<title>CHINA: China PC sales seen growing 40 percent in 1997.</title>
<headline>China PC sales seen growing 40 percent in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's sales of personal computers (PCs) are seen growing by 40 percent in 1997 to 2.25 million units, the Economic Daily said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Some 450,000-500,000 computers would be bought for home use, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Well-known brands of domestic PCs would account for about 32 percent of the market while foreign brands would capture 40 percent, it said.</p>
<p>The software market would swell by 35-40 percent in 1997 while printer sales were seen hitting 1.1 million units, it said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
